          <p>
            Screw-drive openers use a threaded steel rod to move the trolley. They have fewer moving parts but are noisier than belts and can be sluggish in very cold garages, and the major brands have largely stopped making them for the consumer market. If you have one that works, there is no reason to replace it; if you are buying new, choose belt, chain or wall-mount.
          </p>
