          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most attached garages, the Chamberlain B4310 is the opener to buy: a quiet belt drive with a DC motor, built-in battery backup, Wi-Fi and a camera. If your home runs on Alexa or Google, or you want a keypad in the box, the Genie StealthDrive Connect 7155-TKV is the better fit. Tall, heavy or high-lift doors belong on a wall-mount opener like the Chamberlain RJO101.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Before you spend anything, check that the door is balanced and the springs are sound, measure its height and the headroom, and make sure your choice includes battery backup. Get those right and almost any current opener from Chamberlain or Genie will serve you well for a decade or more.
